R"VG(
# song.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the song's register: an event of the history sung (`@event ... song`: the ballads, the
# laments, the old time's songs), in lines (`\n`), with a refrain. Each people sings with its own refrains (`song.refrain`: a people
# keeps its own five), its own beasts, crops, instruments and griefs (the culture pools), so a ballad of a battle is a different song on
# every world. A line of a prehistoric song names nothing a later age made (no bells, no iron). The rest of the register: song_land.vg (the
# land and the sky, the works, the leaving, the everyday); the picture's: picture.vg.

@root song.* picture.*

# =====================================================================================================================
# the refrains: a people's own (a formula: they come back by design)
# =====================================================================================================================

song.refrain (formula people=5)
  sing it low, sing it slow, {god} knows who lies there.
  and the river goes on, and the river goes on.
  oh {city}, {city}, who will remember you.
  turn the cup, turn the cup, and drink to the ones not here.
  and {skyone} saw it, and said nothing.
  so the old ones sing it, and the young ones learn.
  bring the {herd} home, bring the {herd} home, the night is coming down.
  and the {bird} cry over {river}, and nobody answers them.
  weep for them, weep, under {skynight}.
  hold the light, hold the light, {festival} is coming.
  the {tree>.tr} remember it, the {.tr} remember.
  and that is why we wear {colour.mourn}.
  a {beast} for the road and a song for the dead.
  lay it down, lay it down, by {watersrc}.
  and {time.pass}.
  and they have {death.went>.dw}, they have {.dw}.
  {exclaim>.ex}, {.ex}, and fill the cup again.
  fill the {vessel} and drink to them, drink to them all.
  dance the {~dance}, dance it round, and stamp on the hard ground.
  to {instrument>.in}, to {.in}, all the night long.
  {crop} and salt, {crop} and salt, and a fire against the cold.
  and the wind comes down off {mountain}, and the wind comes down.
  {god} have them, {god} have them, we cannot.
  so we sing it at {festival}, and then we go home.
  and the {herd} lie down in the long grass, and the {herd} lie down.
  ho, the {crop}, the {crop}, and the long road home.
  and the {fruit} fall where they fall.
  sing it once for them and once for us.
  let the {~hymn} go up, let it go up.
  and {sea} took the rest, as {sea} does.
  under the {roofs}, under the {roofs}, the children sleep.
  ask {mountain}, {mountain} was there.
  round the fire, round the fire, and nobody leave.

# =====================================================================================================================
# war
# =====================================================================================================================

song.battle
  {ann.sg.bat.a}\n{ann.sg.bat.b}\n{ann.sg.bat.c}\n{song.refrain}
  {ann.sg.bat.a}\n{ann.sg.bat.b}\n{ann.sg.bat.d}\n{ann.sg.bat.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.bat.a
  At {$e.place} in {$e.season} the army stood,
  They went down to {$e.place} with the {crop} still green,
  Who was at {$e.place}? Ask the ones who came home,
  They marched to {$e.place} singing, as the young ones do,
  They left the {herd} with the old and went down to {$e.place},
  We were {ann.craftfolk} and we were {ann.herdfolk}, and we went to {$e.place},
  Early in {$e.season} they took up the spears at {$e.place},
  ($e.won=1) Hear what was done at {$e.place}, hear it and learn,
  (age>=medieval) The {colour.holy} banners went down the road to {$e.place},
  (age=prehistoric) The bands went painted to {$e.place}, painted in {colour.holy},
  They kissed their mothers at the door and went to {$e.place},
ann.sg.bat.b
  ($e.won=1) and the enemy broke like ice on {river};
  ($e.won=1) and by evening the field was ours;
  ($e.won=1) and the others ran, and we let them run;
  ($e.won=1) and the {bird} came down on the others' dead, not ours;
  ($e.won=0) and the field was theirs by night;
  ($e.won=0) and we were too few, and they were too many;
  ($e.won=0) and we came back fewer than we went;
  ($e.won=0) and they drove us down to the water like {herd};
  ($e.won=draw) and neither would give, and both stood till dark;
  ($e.won=draw) and both went home and called it won;
  and the fighting went on until nobody could lift an arm;
ann.sg.bat.c
  ($e.value>0) {#$e.value:about} lay down there and did not rise,
  the {bird} came down on {$e.place} for a week,
  and the mothers of {city} went out in {colour.mourn} to look,
  and what was won there nobody could say over the {drink},
  and the rain came after and washed it into the {crop},
  and the ones who came back went back to the {craft} and did not talk of it,
  and we {ann.sg.buried} them where they fell,
  and the {crop} grows thicker there to this day,
  and the {herd} would not graze that ground again,
ann.sg.bat.d
  and {tool} was put down and the spear taken up,
  and somebody sang, and the others joined in,
  (age>=medieval) and the steel rang all day like a smithy,
  and the dust stood over them like smoke,
  and the shouting was heard as far as {$seat},

# how the dead were put away, as a verb phrase after "we" (the people's custom)
ann.sg.buried
  (deadway=barrows) laid
  (deadway=tombs) carried
  (deadway=cemeteries) buried
  (deadway=towers) carried
  (deadway=none) gave
ann.craftfolk
  (economy=hunting) hunters
  (economy=herding) herders
  (economy=farming) {crop} growers
  (economy=trade) traders
  (economy=industry) mill hands
  (economy=information) clerks
  weavers
  potters
ann.herdfolk
  (economy=herding|economy2=herding) the ones who keep the {herd}
  (economy!=herding) the ones who till the ground
  the young of the river towns

song.sack
  {ann.sg.sack.a}\n{ann.sg.sack.b}\n{ann.sg.sack.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.sack.a
  {$e.place} had a gate and the gate was strong,
  {$e.place} had {roofs} and they burned like straw,
  There was {food} on the tables in {$e.place} that night,
  They came to {$e.place} with fire in {vessel},
ann.sg.sack.b
  and they burned it down in a single night,
  and they took the children and the {herd},
  and what they could not carry they broke,
  and they left {motif.over} black on every wall,
ann.sg.sack.c
  and who was inside, ask the ashes,
  and the {bird} nest there now, and nothing else,
  ($e.value>0) and {#$e.value:about} went down with the walls,
  and nobody lives there, and nobody will,

song.siege
  {ann.sg.siege.a}\n{ann.sg.siege.b}\n{ann.sg.siege.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.siege.a
  They sat outside {$e.place} through {season.now},
  The {ann.foe} camped round {$e.place} like a ring round {ann.moonsun},
  We shut the gates of {$e.place} and counted the {vessel},
ann.sg.siege.b
  we ate the {herd} and then we ate the hides,
  we drank from {watersrc} and it held, it held,
  we burned the doors when the {fuel} was gone,
  we ate the {crop} seed we were keeping for spring,
ann.sg.siege.c
  ($e.out=0) and the gate held, the gate held, and they went home,
  ($e.out=1) and the gate fell, and we were taken,
  ($e.out=1) and in the end we opened the gate ourselves,
  ($e.out=0) and one morning the camp was empty and the fires were cold,
ann.foe
  (contact=1) {other}
  enemy
ann.moonsun
  (moons>0) {moon}
  the sun

song.war
  {ann.sg.war.a}\n{ann.sg.war.b}\n{ann.sg.war.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.war.a
  When {$e.war} began, the young ones sang over the {drink},
  When {$e.war} came, it came in {$e.season},
  They called it {$e.war}, like the name of a feast with {feast.custom},
  Nobody wanted {$e.war}, so everybody went,
ann.sg.war.b
  (age>=medieval) the smiths worked all night, and the {craft} stopped,
  the drums went down the road and the mothers watched from the {roofs},
  (age>=medieval) the {colour.holy} banners went up and the {food} went dear,
  the {herd} were driven up into the hills,
  the {craft} was left half done on every bench,
  the {crop} was cut green so the armies would not have it,
ann.sg.war.c
  and everyone said it would be over by {festival}, with {drink} for all,
  and everyone said it would be over by the {crop} harvest,
  and everyone said it would be over by {season.next}, before the {herd} came down,
  and it lasted longer than anyone who sang it, and longer than the {crop},
  and the ones who said it was glorious stayed at home with their {herd},

# =====================================================================================================================
# the sick
# =====================================================================================================================

song.sickness
  {ann.sg.sick.a}\n{ann.sg.sick.b}\n{ann.sg.sick.c}\n{song.refrain}
  {ann.sg.sick.a}\n{ann.sg.sick.b}\n{ann.sg.sick.d}\n{ann.sg.sick.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.sick.a
  ($e.wave=1) {$e.sickness} came to {$e.place} with the boats,
  {$e.sickness} came in {$e.season}, nobody asked it in,
  ($e.wave>1) {$e.sickness} came back, as it always comes back,
  {$e.sickness} walked into {$e.place} like a guest,
  It came to {$e.place} in {$e.season}, and they named it {$e.sickness},
  {$e.sickness} came down the road from {$e.place},
ann.sg.sick.b
  it sat at every table and ate the {food}, and it slept in every bed,
  it took the old ones first, then the {ann.craftfolk}, then the rest,
  (age>=medieval) and the bells were rung until there was no one to ring them,
  and the {fuel} fires went out one by one along the river,
  and the {herd} stood unmilked in the yards,
  and the {craft} stopped, and the market stopped,
  and the healers went from door to door with {vessel} until they fell,
  and we marked the doors with {colour.any},
ann.sg.sick.c
  ($e.value>0) {#$e.value:about} we carried out to {deadplace},
  and the doors of {$e.place} stood open all that year, and the {herd} walked in,
  and we sang this then, to {instrument}, and we sing it still,
  and the ones it spared went back to the {crop} and did not know why,
  and when it went, it went in a night, the way it came, and the {bird} came back,
ann.sg.sick.d
  my mother, my brother, the child next door who kept the {herd},
  we burned {fuel} in the streets against it,
  we prayed at {holyplace} and it came in with us,

# =====================================================================================================================
# the deaths
# =====================================================================================================================

song.rulerdeath
  {ann.sg.rd.a}\n{ann.sg.rd.b}\n{ann.sg.rd.c}\n{song.refrain}
  {ann.sg.rd.a}\n{ann.sg.rd.b}\n{ann.sg.rd.d}\n{ann.sg.rd.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.rd.a
  (age=prehistoric) {$e.a:full} is dead, and the {fuel} fires are put out for {$e.a:obj},
  (age>=medieval) {$e.a:full} is dead, hang {colour.mourn} on the doors for {$e.a:obj},
  They carried {$e.a:full} out {time.of},
  (age=prehistoric) Who will sit where {$e.a:name} sat, on the {colour.holy} stone by the fire,
  (age>=medieval) Who will sit where {$e.a:name} sat, under {motif.over} at {city},
  {$e.a:name} has gone to {deadplace} and the {herd} are crying,
  (age>=medieval gov=monarchy) The crown of {city} is on another head, and the {herd} do not care,
  (has:$e.a.epithet) {$e.a:name} {$e.a.epithet} is dead at {$e.place}, and the {bird} know it,
  Put on {colour.mourn}, {$e.a:name} is dead,
  {$e.a:full} has {death.went},
  The {ann.instrument.cry} for {$e.a:full}, who is dead at {$e.place},
ann.instrument.cry
  drums are beating
  pipes are crying
  horns are blowing
  songs are going up
ann.sg.rd.b
  (has:$e.a.reigned) {$e.a:name} who held the rule {#$e.a.reigned:words|year} and ate {food} like the rest of us,
  {$e.a:name} who knew every path to {mountain}, every {watersrc.n} and every {tree.n},
  {$e.a:name} who was hard, and was fair, and liked {drink} too much,
  (age=prehistoric) and {$e.a:poss} spear is laid down beside {$e.a:obj}, with {$e.a:poss} {vessel.one.n} of {drink},
  (age>=medieval) and {$e.a:poss} seal is broken in {colour.holy} wax on the steps of {hall},
  (has:$e.a.trait) {$e.a:name} who was {$e.a.trait}, and wore {garment} in every weather,
  {$e.a:name} who gave us {food} in the bad year,
  {$e.a:name} who sat with the {ann.craftfolk} and drank their {drink},
  {$e.a:name} who loved {pastime} and lost at it, and laughed,
  {$e.a:name} who counted the {herd} with us every {season.any},
ann.sg.rd.c
  there was never another like {$e.a:obj} under the {roofs},
  and the next will be no better, and will eat more {food},
  (age=prehistoric) and nobody speaks at the {fuel} fire tonight,
  (age>=medieval) and nobody speaks in {hall} tonight, and the {vessel} stand full,
  and the young ones look at each other over the {vessel} and wait,
  and the women keen in {colour.mourn} at the door till dawn,
  and the new one counts the {herd} and is afraid, and should be,
  and the {bird} sit on the roof of {hall} and say nothing,
  and the {herd} would not go out to the grass that day,
  and the {crop} stood in the field with nobody to cut it,
ann.sg.rd.d
  we {ann.sg.buried} {$e.a:obj} with {$e.a:poss} {garment.n} and a {vessel.one.n} of {drink},
  we played {instrument} until our hands were sore,
  we cut {motif.over} for {$e.a:obj} on the post by the door,
  we burned {fuel} on the grave for {#number|night}, and poured {drink} on it,

song.death
  {ann.sg.death.a}\n{ann.sg.death.b}\n{ann.sg.death.c}\n{song.refrain}
ann.sg.death.a
  {$e.a:full} is gone, who was known to every {ann.craftfolk.one},
  {$e.a:full} has {death.went},
  ($e.a.role!=none) {$e.a:name} the {$e.a.role} is dead at {$e.place}, and the {bird} know it,
  They carried {$e.a:full} out at {ann.hour}, in {colour.mourn},
  Who will do it now that {$e.a:name} is gone, who will see to the {herd},
  Hang {colour.mourn} on the door, {$e.a:name} is dead,
ann.sg.death.b
  they carried {$e.a:obj} up to {deadplace} on a bed of {material},
  the town came out to see {$e.a:obj} go, and the {herd} came too,
  we put {$e.a:poss} {garment.n} round {$e.a:obj} against the cold,
  and {$e.a:poss} {ann.tooln} hangs on the wall and nobody takes it down,
  ($e.how=sickness has:$e.sickness) {$e.sickness} took {$e.a:obj} in {$e.season}, before the {crop} was in,
  ($e.how=battle) {$e.a:name} went to the fighting and did not come back to the {herd},
  ($e.how=sea) {sea} has {$e.a:obj}, and keeps {$e.a:obj}, and gives back {ann.seagift},
  ($e.how=old) {$e.a:name} was old, and tired, and ready, and had eaten {food} that morning,
ann.sg.death.c
  and the house is quiet where {$e.a:name} used to play {instrument},
  and the dogs look for {$e.a:obj} at the door of {ann.house1},
  and we will not see the like again, not if the {crop} comes up gold,
  and {$e.a:poss} children have {$e.a:poss} eyes, and {$e.a:poss} way with the {herd},
  and the {vessel.one.n} {$e.a:name} drank from is turned over on the shelf,
ann.craftfolk.one
  hunter
  herder
  weaver
  potter
  boatman
  child
ann.seagift
  (coast=1) {fish}
  driftwood
ann.hour
  first light
  dusk
  noon
  lamp-lighting
ann.tooln
  (age<=prehistoric) spear
  (age<=prehistoric) net
  adze
  sickle
  hoe
  (age>=medieval) hammer
  (age>=medieval) knife
)VG"
